# Learn → Tables

Tables for looking a form up. Nothing here teaches: every rule is explained in a guide (`src/routes/guides/`), and each table links to the guide section that teaches it. Public: no auth guard. This was the Reference section until it folded into Learn.

## Route Structure

```
/learn/tables/:tab            $tab.tsx: articles, nouns, pronouns, adjectives
/learn/tables/verbs           verbs/route.tsx layout (own route family, not a :tab)
/learn/tables/verbs/          redirects to /learn/tables/verbs/present
/learn/tables/verbs/:band     present, past, past-continuous, future
/reference/*                  old addresses: src/routes/reference/$.tsx redirects each (301)
                              through REFERENCE_REDIRECTS (reference/redirects.data.ts)
```

- `$tab.tsx` checks `VALID_TABS`; any other `:tab` throws `notFound()` (404).
- `head` sets the document title from the tab's `TABLES_TABS` label; a verb band's title is "Verbs: <band label>".
- Every tab and band renders a `BackLink` to /learn, then `TablesNav` (a `NavTabs` bar over `TABLES_TABS`), above its content.
- `src/routes/route-paths.test.ts` checks that every redirect target and every guide's table link is a real route.

## Page shape

Every tab and verb band has the same shape, from `components/lookup-section.tsx`:

- `LookupPage`: `PageHeading` with the title and the one line "Tables for looking a form up. The rules are in the guides."
- One `LookupSection` per table, in a fixed order: an `h2`, a `GrammarTable` of `GreekText` cells with no case colours, and "Taught in: <guide section title> →" links.
- Nothing else: no hero, teaching cards, quizzes, mistakes or next-step cards.

`TAUGHT_IN` in `taught-in.data.ts` holds every guide section a table links to, with its title copied from the guide, so the pages never import the guide data. `src/routes/guides/guide-forms.test.ts` checks each entry against the guide's real section id and title.

## Tabs

<tab route="/learn/tables/pronouns" file="tabs/pronouns.tsx">
One table, "Every pronoun form", from `constants/pronouns.ts` (nothing generates pronouns). Links to little-words: forms, objects, long forms.
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/tables/articles" file="tabs/articles.tsx">
One table, "The article, every form", rendered from `getArticle` (`src/lib/greek-grammar.ts`) through `gender-case-table.tsx`. Links to roles: articles, plural.
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/tables/nouns" file="tabs/nouns.tsx">
One table per gender, from `AGREEMENT_PARADIGMS` (`constants/agreement.ts`, the same source as `declineNoun`), each pattern with example words from the DB (`getNounsForPatternTables`, loaded by `$tab.tsx`). Links to the nouns guide's family sections.
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/tables/adjectives" file="tabs/adjectives.tsx">
Three tables from `declineAdjective` (`src/lib/adjective-declension.ts`): καλός (-ος, -η, -ο), ωραίος (-ος, -α, -ο), βαρύς (-ύς, -ιά, -ύ). Links to the agreement guide.
</tab>

## Verb bands

<route path="/learn/tables/verbs/:band">
<file>src/routes/learn/tables/verbs/$band.tsx; tables in components/verb-tables.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: `getVerbTablesFn` (`src/server/fns/verb-tables.ts`) loads every tense of the band's example verbs (`bandLemmas`), with their ids. Each verb's name, in a column header or a stem-table row, links to /learn/verbs/:verbId.</data-source>
<displays>
`BAND_TABLES` lists each band's tables, their example verbs and the guide section each links to. The families follow the verbs guide:

- present: γράφω, μιλάω and the πάω set; πάω and τρώω endings; stressed -ώ; -μαι; -άμαι; είμαι
- past: simple past endings; stems with σ, ψ and ξ; four groups with a past of their own; -μαι; είμαι
- past continuous: regular; -άω and -ώ; verbs that add γ; own-past verbs; -μαι; είμαι
- future: θα and the short form; three sets of own short forms; two tables with no separate short form; -μαι
</displays>
<note>`src/routes/guides/guide-verb-forms.test.ts` checks the guides' verb tables against `generateConjugations`.</note>
</route>
